-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",343,{
[10945]="700431B6\n1\tGuards can be found throughout Tumladen, especially near the refugees of Minas Tirith. Her curiosity appeased, Lady Terenis has asked you to scold the guards of Tumladen that are spreading rumours about the battle at Pelargir.\t\n2\tTalk to Lady Terenis\tLady Terenis can be found in her hall in Tumladen. You have scolded several guards and sent them back to their posts. You should now return to Lady Terenis.\n",
[10946]="700375D2\n1\tCollect horseshoes (total: 16)\tHorseshoes might be found at the Edoras stables. Léofdag asked you to collect new horseshoes for the Riders' mounts.\n2\tShoe Brynmód\030Shoe Flyting\030Shoe Gesith\030Shoe Hafoc\tBrynmód, Flyting, Gesith, and Hafoc -- the horses of the Riders Four -- are in Edoras. Léofdag asked you to fit the Riders' horses with the new shoes.\n3\tTalk to Léofdag\tLéofdag is in Edoras. You should return to Léofdag and let him know that you have done as he requested.\n",
[10947]="70066941\n1\tHungry sea-gulls flock to Melgobas to steal Rindur's hard-earned fish. You should shoo them away.\t\n2\tTalk to Rindur\tYou've scared off the sea-gulls... for now. You should let Rindur know. He can be found in Melgobas.\n",
[10948]="700700B1\n1\tShoo shrews (total: 8)\030Destroy shrew nests (total: 8)\tNila has asked you to shoo the shrews away and destroy their nests to encourage them to leave. The shrews are inside the tunnel located south-east of the Staddle village centre.\n2\tTalk to Nila Brambleberry\tYou have shoo'd away the shrews and destroyed their nests as Nila Brambleberry requested. You should return to her just outside the cave entrance, south-east of the Staddle village centre.\n",
[10949]="700561E0\n1\tRoar to shoo rabbits in the fields (total: 6)\tRabbits can be found throughout the neighbourhoods of the Rohan Kingstead. You should shoo rabbits out of the gardens.\n",
[10950]="70000D50\n1\tBring field stones to Belco Brockhouse\030Collect flat field-stones (total: 3)\030Collect small field-stones (total: 4)\030Collect large field-stones (total: 2)\tField stones can be found south of Longo Burrow's farm near the big willow. Belco lives north-west of the willow, on the upper slopes of Tuckborough. Belco Brockhouse's fences need mending, and he has asked you to gather stones from the field for him to use in patching them.\n",
[10951]="700265B9\n1\tCollect rubble (total: 6)\tThe rubble is just to the east of Echad Garthadir.\n2\tBring the rubble to Orchalwë\tOrchalwë may have a use for the rubble.\n",
[10952]="7005338F\n1\tCollect shorn beards from the Shapag-hai at Lúlstrok\t\n2\tCollect shorn beards from the Shapag-hai at Lúlstrok (total: 20)\tShorn dwarf-beards are worn by the Shapag-hai at Lúlstrok in the north-western reaches of the Gladden Fields. You have noticed a number of Shapag-hai wearing the beards of slain dwarves as trophies on their armour. You should defeat them and take the dwarf-beards to be burned.\n3\tBurn the shorn dwarf-beards in a camp-fire at Lúlstrok\tCamp-fires can be found in Lúlstrok in the north-western reaches of the Gladden Fields. You have collected a number of shorn dwarf-beards from the Shapag-hai. To keep them out of the hands of the Orcs, you should burn them in a camp-fire at Lúlstrok.\n4\tCompleted\tYou have burned the dwarf-beards kept as trophies by the Shapag-hai.\n",
[10953]="7002EF52\n1\tTalk to Hestil and begin the rescue of Drafli Broadshield\tHestil is at her camp on Parth Galen. Hestil is waiting for you to let her know when you are ready to begin the rescue attempt of Drafli Broadshield.\n2\tTalk to Hestil\tHestil is at her camp on Parth Galen. You have aided in the rescue of Drafli Broadshield and should now speak to Hestil.\n",
[10954]="7002BFC6\n1\tTalk to Amal when you are ready to confront the Khundolar\tAmal is at the Woodman camp in the heart of the Rushgore. You should speak with Amal when you are ready to depart for the Easterling camp. NOTE: This instance quest is meant to be run Solo and cannot be run in a group.\n2\tTalk to Amal at the Woodman camp in the Rushgore\tAmal is at the Woodman camp in the heart of the Rushgore. You should return to Amal with news of your victory over the Easterlings.\n",
[10955]="7002BFC7\n1\tDefeat Nafrati\tTo secure the safety of the Woodmen, you should defeat Nafrati.\n",
[10956]="700561E6\n1\tFind the children who wish to see your ranged skills\tChildren can be found at the target range in the Rohan Kingstead neighbourhoods. You should find the children who wish to be entertained.\n2\tShow off your ranged skills (total: 3)\tChildren can be found at the target range in the Rohan Kingstead neighbourhoods. You should show off your ranged skills. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[10957]="70062DD3\n1\tShoo the shrews in the orchard north of Nerys Trafferth's house (total: 4)\tThe orchard to the north of Nerys Trafferth's home is full of shrews to be shooed.\n2\tThe shrews are gone... but only for now\tThere is no end to the shrews in the orchard.\n3\tTalk to Nerys Trafferth in Lintrev\tNerys Trafferth is outside her house in Lintrev.\n4\tSet down the apple basket near the bottom of the hill north of Nerys Trafferth's orchard\tNerys asked you to place the apple basket a good distance down the hill north of her orchard.\n5\tTalk to Nerys Trafferth in Lintrev\tNerys Trafferth is outside her house in Lintrev.\n",
[10958]="70060DA3\n1\tCollect all the stolen map scraps (total: 8)\tFrothard's map was stolen and torn up by shrews in Yondershire. You should collect all the stolen map scraps from shrews in Yondershire.\n2\tBring the map scraps to Frothard Took\tFrothard Took can be found in the Village of Tighfield. You should bring the map scraps to Frothard Took.\n3\tFind the hidden treasure\tThe location of the hidden treasure is in the woods east of the village of Gamwich. You should find the hidden treasure.\n4\tDig up the hidden treasure\tThe location of the hidden treasure is in the woods east of the village of Gamwich. You should dig up the hidden treasure.\n5\tOpen the old coffer and remove the treasure inside\tThe location of the hidden treasure is in the woods east of the village of Gamwich. You should open the old coffer and remove the treasure inside.\n6\tBring the golf clubs to Frothard Took\tFrothard Took can be found in the village of Tighfield. You should bring the golf clubs to Frothard Took.\n",
[10959]="7004AB95\n1\tDefeat foes at Magh Nûl (total: 6)\030Defeat foes at Magh Groth (total: 6)\tGhâsh-hai can be found at Magh Nûl and Magh Groth. You should defeat foes at these locations.\n",
[10960]="700509C0\n1\tDefeat Shákoth, Scourge of Glimmerdeep\tShákoth poses a great threat to all that attempt to remove resources while under his watch in Glimmerdeep.\n2\tDefeat Shákoth, Scourge of Glimmerdeep\tShákoth poses a great threat to all that attempt to remove resources while under his watch in Glimmerdeep.\n3\tCompleted\tShákoth poses a great threat to all that attempt to remove resources while under his watch in Glimmerdeep.\n",
[10961]="700453D8\n1\tFind and defeat Shákrug\tShákrug's stronghold is located in Maudhúl Grak. You should find and defeat Shákrug.\n2\tFind and defeat Shákrug\tShákrug's stronghold is located in Maudhúl Grak. You should find and defeat Shákrug.\n3\tRescue Bregdal\tBregdal is in Shákrug's stronghold. You should rescue Bregdal.\n4\tSpeak with Bregdal outside of Maudhúl Grak\tBregdal is outside of Maudhúl Grak. You should speak with Bregdal.\n5\tSpeak with Ghân-buri-Ghân\tGhân-buri-Ghân can be found in Drû Bhûta. You should return to Ghân-buri-Ghân with the head of Shákrug.\n",
[10962]="70027E94\n1\tSpoil White Hand food-stores (total: 12)\tFood-stores can be found within the White Hand encampment in Trum Dreng. You should break into the encampment and spoil all the food-stores you find there.\n2\tReturn to Guto at his encampment\tGuto is at his small encampment in the southern fields of Trum Dreng. You should return to Guto with news of your success.\n",
[10963]="7000732E\n1\tDefeat spiders in Eastern Haudh Lin (total: 12)\tSpiders infest north-eastern Haudh Lin, far beyond Duillond. Laergil has asked you to kill off as many spiders as you are able.\n2\tTalk to Laergil\tLaergil waits in north-western Haudh Lin. You should return to Laergil and report your success.\n",
[10964]="700669D3\n1\tDefeat gelin sickle-flies (total: 8)\tBranach has asked you to defeat sickle flies. The sickle-flies in question can be found to the south-west of Branach's farm, Cornworth.\n2\tTalk to Branach\tYou have done as Branach asked. Return to him. Branach can be found at his farm, Cornworth, north-west of Gnatstead.\n",
[10965]="7006301E\n1\tDefeat reed-munching sickle-flies (total: 10)\tAerona has asked you to reduce the number of sickle-flies buzzing about the ponds and waterways east of Herne. Herne is in western Cardolan.\n2\tReturn to Aerona\tYou should let Aerona know that fewer sickle-flies will trouble the reeds of the ponds near Herne. Aerona is in Herne.\n",
[10966]="7002EFEE\n1\tExplore the northernmost chamber off the tunnel\030Explore the middle chamber off the tunnel\030Explore the southernmost chamber off the tunnel\tIsteron wants you to thoroughly map the three side passages that branch off the main tunnel that runs beneath the East Wall.\n2\tTalk to Isteron\tIsteron is by the northernmost exit from the caves that run beneath the East Wall. You have explored the side passages beneath the East Wall's main passage and should return to Isteron with the information you have collected.\n",
[10967]="70039757\n1\tTalk to Herefara\tTalk to Herefara to aid the defence of Brockbridge.\n2\tTalk to Herefara\tHerefara is in Brockbridge. Herefara would like to thank you for your aid in the battle.\n",
[10968]="700381BF\n1\tDefeat the waves of attackers at the tower base ([see journal]/10)\tSaruman's forces have sent out their siege weapons to wreak havoc upon the battlefront. While the men on the wall focus on surviving the boulders raining down upon them, foes have crept into the deep and are planning on using black powder to destroy one of the siege-towers from below. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[10969]="70053F4E\n1\tRepair siege equipment at Adambel (total: 10)\tSiege equipment in disrepair can be found at Adambel. You should repair the siege equipment.\n2\tTalk to Eärtur\tEärtur can be found at Adambel. You should talk to Eärtur.\n",
[10970]="70030A36\n1\tDestroy catapults (total: 4)\tCatapults can be found among the enemy forces at Eaworth. The catapults being used by the uruks assaulting Eaworth must be destroyed if the town is to be secured.\n2\tTalk to Dernstan\tDernstan is at Eaworth. Dernstan will be pleased to hear that you have dismantled several catapults.\n",
[10971]="7002F30B\n1\tDefeat the Uruks besieging Eaworth (total: 10)\tUruks are besieging Eaworth. Dernstan asked you to aid in defending Eaworth from the Uruks encamped to the south.\n2\tTalk to Dernstan\tDernstan is at Eaworth. Dernstan will be pleased to hear that you defeated many Uruks while defending Eaworth.\n",
[10972]="7002F307\n1\tDefeat goblins and Wargs near Faldham (total: 10)\tGoblins and Wargs can be found at the farmsteads around Faldham. Aldbéort asked you to aid in the defence of Faldham.\n2\tTalk to Aldbéort\tAldbéort is at Cliving. Aldbéort will be pleased to hear Faldham has been defended and the attackers driven back.\n",
[10973]="7002FA69\n1\tBring water to the central farmhouse\030Bring water to the south-west farmhouse\030Bring water to the north-east farmhouse\030Bring water to the east farmhouse\030Bring water to the north farmhouse\tBurning houses can be found at farmsteads around Faldham. Aldbéort has asked you to aid in the defence of Faldham by bringing water to burning farmsteads.\n2\tTalk to Aldbéort\tAldbéort is at Cliving. Aldbéort will be pleased to hear that you helped put out the fires.\n",
[10974]="70029FBD\n1\tComplete 'Siege of Gondamon' in a raid group\tGondamon is one of the strongest fortresses of the Longbeards in the Blue Mountains. The Dourhands and their goblin-allies seek to overthrow the stronghold and claim it for themselves.\n",
[10975]="70043045\n1\tDestroy Ballistae (total: 3)\030Destroy Catapults (total: 6)\030Destroy Trebuchets (total: 5)\tSiege equipment can be found just outside of Osgiliath in Southern Ithilien. You should destroy the siege equipment before it can be conveyed across the river.\n2\tCompleted\tDestroyed the siege equipment.\n",
[10976]="7003A490\n1\tDefeat White Hand trolls (0/3)\tThe pungent and unmistakable odour of troll fills your nostrils, and a small shiver of fear creeps up your spine. There must be one or more close by. You should deal with them before they become too great a threat.\n2\tDefeat White Hand trolls (total: 3)\tThe pungent and unmistakable odour of troll fills your nostrils, and a small shiver of fear creeps up your spine. There must be one or more close by. You should deal with them before they become too great a threat.\n3\tComplete\tTrolls are among the more feared weapons of the Enemy. They were bred for war and can devastate a front line, break through barricades or defences, and can bring down structures as well as any ballistae.\n",
})
